d3d9: a pixel shader's push constants are declared with their size

src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp
- compileShader() gave the shader's push constant size as its offset
  (info.pushConstSize = m_pushConstOffset). For pixel shaders older than 3.0 the offset is 0,
  so they declared no push constants at all, though they read the render state from them
  (fog, the alpha test's reference value). The pipeline layout then has no push constant
  range for the fragment stage. Drivers on Windows and Linux do not mind; MoltenVK binds push
  constants only to the stages the layout names, the Metal shader read a buffer that was not
  bound ("Fragment Function(main0): missing Buffer binding at index 1 for render_state[0]"
  with Metal's validation on), and the GPU gave the whole command buffer up: "Lost VkDevice
  ... Internal Error". Portal 2 froze as its first level loaded.

tests/runtime/d3d9-draw.c draws with the alpha test on under a 2.0 pixel shader.

diff --git a/src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp b/src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp
index 7cd6f72..6695a79 100644
--- a/src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp
+++ b/src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp
@@ -253,7 +253,7 @@ namespace dxvk {
     info.inputMask = m_inputMask;
     info.outputMask = m_outputMask;
     info.pushConstOffset = m_pushConstOffset;
-    info.pushConstSize = m_pushConstOffset;
+    info.pushConstSize = m_pushConstSize;
 
     return new DxvkShader(info, m_module.compile());
   }
